From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stepcompress: bump QUEUE_START_SIZE 1024 -> 2048

Matches the FlashForge fork of Klipper v0.11.0 (the only
behavioural-but-not-cosmetic delta in their fork outside the chelper
runtime-build-check disable).  Saves one realloc-and-memcpy per
stepper queue at the start of operation, at the cost of allocating
twice as many initial slots upfront (~5-10 KB across the AD5M's five
steppers; trivial).

Upstream Klipper still ships 1024 on master, v0.11.0, v0.12.0;
FlashForge picked 2048 in their AD5M-Series-Klipper fork at first
commit and has shipped it across the entire AD5M user base since
2024-01.  No upstream PR thread to back-link.

This is the only FF-fork behavioural delta we adopt by default
beyond patch 0001 (chelper build-check).  See the FF fork deltas
catalog in docs/research/2026-06-04-klipper-v0.11-fork-deltas.md
for the other 4 (which we deliberately skip).

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
---
 klippy/chelper/stepcompress.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/klippy/chelper/stepcompress.c b/klippy/chelper/stepcompress.c
--- a/klippy/chelper/stepcompress.c
+++ b/klippy/chelper/stepcompress.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #include "stepcompress.h" // stepcompress_alloc
 
 #define CHECK_LINES 1
-#define QUEUE_START_SIZE 1024
+#define QUEUE_START_SIZE 2048
 
 struct stepcompress {
     // Buffer management
-- 
2.47.0
